    "source": "IRS Revenue Procedure 2025-32 \u00a74.01 (rate tables) and \u00a74.14 (standard deduction)",
    "note": "Taken from the Revenue Procedure PDF itself, not the newsroom summary. That matters: the IRS newsroom article implies Married Filing Separately shares Single's 640,600 top threshold, but Table 4 puts MFS at 384,350 (half of MFJ). Head of Household also differs subtly from Single at the 24%/32% boundaries (201,750/256,200 vs 201,775/256,225)."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Bands are ABSOLUTE boundaries on taxable income (gross minus the standard deduction), matching the UK convention so `calculateProgressiveTax` can be reused unchanged.",
    "Standard deduction is applied before the bands; it is NOT a 0% first band.",
    "Additional standard deduction for aged/blind (1,650, or 2,050 if unmarried and not a surviving spouse) is not modelled."
